I built the circuit on a breadboard using the given components. I connected a 9 volt battery as the power supply and placed components including resistors, wires, and an LED on the board.
I wired the circuit step by step by connecting the power rails first, then adding resistors and jumper wires to create the signal path. I made sure all components were properly connected across the breadboard rows.
I tested the circuit by powering it on and observing the LED behavior. The LED turned on when the circuit conditions were met, showing that current was flowing correctly through the circuit.
